@prefix math: <http://seanchatmangpt.github.io/packs/tex-math#> .
@prefix log:  <http://www.w3.org/2000/10/swap/log#> .

# ?x is a DanglingCitation if it cites ?y via math:dependsOn or
# math:justification, and ?y is nowhere in the graph the subject of a
# math:kind triple (i.e. ?y does not name a math:Statement individual).
#
# Negation-as-failure idiom: `<> log:semantics ?G` binds ?G to this
# document's own parsed graph (data + rules, since paper_factory_engine's
# n3_closure concatenates them into one file before invoking eye); testing
# `?G log:notIncludes { pattern }` against that bound graph term is the
# form verified to give correct per-binding negation with this EYE version
# (v11.23.1) — the more commonly documented `() log:notIncludes (...)`
# idiom was verified BUGGY here: with more than one candidate binding for
# the negated variable in a single rule body, it evaluates the builtin once
# and incorrectly applies a stale result to every binding (verified via a
# minimal 3-triple reproduction before writing this rule).
{
    ?x math:dependsOn ?y .
    <> log:semantics ?G .
    ?G log:notIncludes { ?y math:kind ?k . } .
} => { ?x a math:DanglingCitation . } .

{
    ?x math:justification ?y .
    <> log:semantics ?G .
    ?G log:notIncludes { ?y math:kind ?k . } .
} => { ?x a math:DanglingCitation . } .
